The internal dimensions of a drink container, in the shape of a rectangular prism, are shown.

\exfigure{36_q23_1}

To completely fill the container with the tropical drink, how many litres of mango juice are required?

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{36_q27_s1}

Using the trapezoidal rule on each of the two strips, with the scale giving a width of $20$ m for each:
$$\begin{aligned} A &\approx \dfrac{20}{2}(25+20)+\dfrac{20}{2}(20+20) \\ &= 850\ \text{m}^2 \end{aligned}$$
